WEBVTT

00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:13,260
In your book, you have a section on GCMAM.

00:00:13,260 --> 00:00:19,260
What is your current recommendation with GCMAM for a patient with double-hit lymphoma?

00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:22,260
What are your current results from using this treatment?

00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:24,260
What is the current availability?

00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:34,260
And where, if this is a viable approach, what testing, AMOS, or NAGELACE, is recommended track progress?

00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:40,260
Well, we can see a fast answer, because we don't use GCMAM.

00:00:40,260 --> 00:00:43,260
It's considered an invasive treatment legally.

00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:44,260
We can't use it.

00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:47,260
Now, there are some other clinics that are getting GCMAM.

00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:52,260
We've had discussions about this for a number of years.

00:00:52,260 --> 00:00:58,260
The place that it gritted where they made it was shut down.

00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:07,260
Somebody on the last Zoom call mentioned that that company has restarted again, maybe a different European country.

00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:09,260
I don't remember what the answer to that was.

00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:11,260
And you can get it again.

00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:18,260
The GCM that was available in the between years was out of the Philippines.

00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:24,260
A lot of doctors that I know that we're using it said the results went drastically.

00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:28,260
So they didn't think that it was an equivalent product.

00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:34,260
So you will have to contact a different clinic about getting GCMAM because we don't have them.

